00:11:21.633 --> 00:11:24.457
- [Voiceover] Matt asks,
"What are your thoughts on

00:11:24.457 --> 00:11:27.728
"employee retention in the
digital marketing industry?

00:11:27.728 --> 00:11:29.496
"Is the high turnover normal?"

00:11:29.496 --> 00:11:31.527
- The reason there's high turnover in my

00:11:31.527 --> 00:11:32.929
industry agency life

00:11:32.929 --> 00:11:35.631
is because most companies are
owned by holding companies

00:11:35.631 --> 00:11:36.708
who are required--

00:11:36.708 --> 00:11:39.694
So there's four major holding
companies in advertising.

00:11:39.694 --> 00:11:41.828
They've consolidated and
bought up all the agencies

00:11:41.828 --> 00:11:43.839
and they are these big
billion dollar conglomerates.

00:11:43.839 --> 00:11:44.876
And I don't know everything about it

00:11:44.876 --> 00:11:46.217
because I haven't really studied it

00:11:46.217 --> 00:11:48.309
but they're big holding
companies which tell companies

00:11:48.309 --> 00:11:51.254
like VaynerMedia, great
companies like 72 and Sunny,

00:11:51.254 --> 00:11:53.592
Great Digital shop and TV Shop.

00:11:53.592 --> 00:11:56.090
Like Jeroga 5 just got
sold, great company.

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:57.879
360 I.

00:11:57.879 --> 00:11:59.748
Carrot that got bought by Vice.

00:11:59.748 --> 00:12:01.150
They're owned by holding companies

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.308
who tell their CEO's,

00:12:02.308 --> 00:12:04.481
usually the guy or gal that looks like me

00:12:04.481 --> 00:12:06.004
that's sold the company for a lot of money

00:12:06.004 --> 00:12:08.057
to get up front but then
you have to earn it out.

00:12:08.057 --> 00:12:10.150
Then you're locked in
because half your money's

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:11.491
gonna come after four years.

00:12:11.491 --> 00:12:13.401
So you gotta keep the
job, golden handcuffs.

00:12:13.401 --> 00:12:14.945
Google it if you don't know what I mean.

00:12:14.945 --> 00:12:17.808
And so they tell them you
have to run your company

00:12:17.808 --> 00:12:19.455
at a 27 percent gross margin

00:12:19.455 --> 00:12:20.715
or 23 percent gross margin.

00:12:20.715 --> 00:12:22.645
You know if I had to do that tomorrow

00:12:22.645 --> 00:12:23.661
because I wanted the big cash out

00:12:23.661 --> 00:12:26.607
I'd probably have to fire 100 people.

00:12:26.607 --> 00:12:29.065
And then what happens
is the inevitable thing

00:12:29.065 --> 00:12:30.406
that looks like this.

00:12:30.406 --> 00:12:32.072
You know you have a superstar youngster

00:12:32.072 --> 00:12:34.530
that's growing up within the organization.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.606
And you guys have lived this.

00:12:35.606 --> 00:12:38.797
So many have gone from making very little

00:12:38.797 --> 00:12:40.829
to making more and more and more, right?

00:12:40.829 --> 00:12:43.531
You inevitably don't promote
them for a year or two

00:12:43.531 --> 00:12:45.786
because you can't afford
to because the only rule

00:12:45.786 --> 00:12:49.301
is you've gotta make 23.7
percent gross profit.

00:12:49.301 --> 00:12:50.967
The only rule.

00:12:50.967 --> 00:12:52.897
And so the reason there's huge turnover

00:12:52.897 --> 00:12:55.376
is because the best people
don't get compensated

00:12:55.376 --> 00:12:56.717
fast enough.

00:12:56.717 --> 00:13:01.410
Nobody who's running the
company has long term ambitions.

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:03.239
Because they've already sold out

00:13:03.239 --> 00:13:05.393
and they're trying to stay
there for 3-4 more years.

00:13:05.393 --> 00:13:07.343
And maximize their bonuses and their money

00:13:07.343 --> 00:13:08.908
so they're making the decision.

00:13:08.908 --> 00:13:10.928
And so like anything in life
everything stems from the top.

00:13:10.928 --> 00:13:12.097
That's what I always say on the show

00:13:12.097 --> 00:13:13.397
and what I said yesterday in
front of the whole company.

00:13:13.397 --> 00:13:14.820
Everything is my fault.

00:13:14.820 --> 00:13:16.425
And that's true in these scenarios

00:13:16.425 --> 00:13:18.599
so this has been a huge
advantage for my company.

00:13:18.599 --> 00:13:20.996
I'm able to do what I'm doing because

00:13:20.996 --> 00:13:22.926
I want to build and
evergreen company forever.

00:13:22.926 --> 00:13:25.302
So I'm able to treat--

00:13:25.302 --> 00:13:27.801
I'm able to deploy meritocracy.

00:13:27.801 --> 00:13:29.407
And if that comes in my expense, it comes

00:13:29.407 --> 00:13:30.464
in my short term expense.

00:13:30.464 --> 00:13:32.252
But fifteen years from
now out of happiness

00:13:32.252 --> 00:13:34.243
and financial, I'll win.

00:13:34.243 --> 00:13:35.503
So that's why that's happening.

00:13:35.503 --> 00:13:38.205
And because they don't want to pay

00:13:38.205 --> 00:13:40.053
and because they run a margin
they do a lot of things.

00:13:40.053 --> 00:13:42.085
They don't compensate people properly.

00:13:42.085 --> 00:13:42.979
They leave.

00:13:42.979 --> 00:13:44.808
They burn good people to the ground.

00:13:44.808 --> 00:13:46.047
You know what goes on here.

00:13:46.047 --> 00:13:47.082
You're in the trenches.

00:13:47.082 --> 00:13:48.587
If somebody's on a hardcore
account that's tough

00:13:48.587 --> 00:13:51.086
you know we usually get them
out of there a year later

00:13:51.086 --> 00:13:52.467
